  chain="Root cells actively take up ions, so water moves into the root from the soil and pushes a column of water up the xylem, but this root pressure alone is not enough for tall plants -> evaporation of water from the leaves, transpiration, creates a suction that pulls water up from the roots -> root pressure matters more at night, while by day with open stomata transpiration pull is the major driving force",
